- Mysterious Name — name does not reveal what it does. → rename.
- Duplicated Code — same logic shape in more than one hunk. → extract.
- Feature Envy — method reaches into another object's data more than its own. → move it.
- Data Clumps — same few fields keep travelling together. → bundle into a type.
- Primitive Obsession — primitive standing in for a domain concept. → give it a type.
- Repeated Switches — same switch/if-cascade on the same type recurs. → polymorphism or one map.
- Shotgun Surgery — one logical change forces scattered edits. → gather into one module.
- Divergent Change — one file edited for several unrelated reasons. → split.
- Speculative Generality — abstraction/hooks the spec doesn't have. → delete.
- Message Chains — long a.b().c().d() the caller shouldn't depend on. → hide the walk.
- Middle Man — class/function that mostly delegates. → cut it.
